<!--
  DJ TechTools Midi Fighter Twister: a Cadence profile from the online library (A208).

  SOURCE, and only this: the manufacturer's own MIDI documentation.
    Midi Fighter Twister - User Guide 2026 (DJ TechTools (linked as "User Guide" from https://store.djtechtools.com/pages/midi-fighter-setup/midi-fighter-twister), 2026 (PDF created 2026-06-01)), pages 2 (channel numbering), 3 (Fig 1 Hardware Naming Convention), 4 (encoders, push switches), 15-16 (switch actions, MIDI type, default channels), 17 (Appendix 1, Bank 1 MIDI)
    https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B-QvIds_FsH3Z0ZLT041VnZfOTA/view
  No mapping file from any other application was read or used.

  status="manual": the message is the manufacturer's. Nobody has tried this map on the hardware
  yet. If a control does nothing, use Learn on that row and tell us at shlabs.contact@gmail.com.
  label="..." is the control's name on the unit, shown in the mapping dialog and the guided tour.

  BEFORE YOU START: Factory defaults (Midi Fighter Utility: Tools > Factory Reset), Bank 1 selected.

  LEFT OUT (no Cadence target): Push switches of encoders 1-12 (CC0-11 on channel 2): left free.; Six side buttons (Bank 1 CC/notes 8-13 on the System channel, 4): left free. Two of them change banks by default, and the guide does not state the default message type of the other four.; Banks 2-4 (encoder CC16-63): this profile assumes Bank 1.; Shift-encoder messages (channel 5), bank-change CCs (channel 4, CC0-7), LED animation channels: not inputs Cadence needs.

  A jog wheel that moves too fast or too slow: set its row to Fine, or invert it, in the dialog.
-->
